     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day, which is about double the maximum daily dose (typically 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release). Exceeding that carries a real risk of lactic acidosis. The dose also doesn't match standard tablet strengths (500, 850, and 1000 mg).\n\nThis may be a typo, such as 500 mg or 850 mg, or the intended total dose may differ. Because I can't tell what the prescriber intended, I won't guess at a corrected dose.\n\nPlease have the prescribing physician review and re-enter the order with the intended dose. Orders like this need to come from a licensed clinician. If you tell me the confirmed drug, dose, route, and frequency, I can enter it. Please also confirm with the physician that the patient's renal function and glucose-lowering indication have been reviewed."
      }
     ],
