      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the dose. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day, roughly double the usual maximum, and an order in the system could be dispensed or administered as written.\n\nTo proceed:\n\n- **Have the prescribing physician re-enter or verify the order.** A physician or pharmacist should review the dose before it goes in. If the physician confirms a dose within the labeled maximum for the formulation, I can enter it.\n- **Ask the physician to check the intended dose.** Common intended doses would be 500 mg, 850 mg, or 1000 mg, but the choice should be theirs.\n- **Notify the pharmacy and medicine team** if this order is already active anywhere in the system, so it can be stopped before the next dose.\n\nIf you can get the physician to confirm a specific dose and frequency, send it to me and I'll enter it with a note recording the clinician's verification."
      }
